<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>Ozakboy.TradeKit.Shioaji</PackageId>
    <AssemblyName>Ozakboy.TradeKit.Shioaji</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>Ozakboy.TradeKit.Shioaji</RootNamespace>

    <Title>Ozakboy.TradeKit.Shioaji — 永豐金 Shioaji 本機 HTTP server 用戶端</Title>
    <Description>永豐金 Shioaji 官方本機 HTTP server(shioaji server start)的 .NET 10 用戶端,建構在 Ozakboy.Http 的管線與 Ozakboy.Security 的遮罩器之上,不使用任何第三方社群套件。本版涵蓋台股當沖桌面系統的第一個里程碑:啟動與監督官方 server 行程、查詢帳號與商品、訂閱行情並讀取串流、下單與查委託。0.2.0 加入歷史資料(ShioajiHistoryClient):1 分 K、逐筆、快照、全市場日 OHLCV、排行掃描、借券券源、資券餘額、處置股與注意股;1 分 K 單次區間超過 30 天與快照超過 500 檔在本地就拒絕;「欄位陣列」回應(datetime[]、Open[] 這種每個欄位一條陣列)任一欄位長度不一致就整筆失敗,絕不送出缺半邊的資料;每日流量超量時券商不報錯、只回空值,所以回傳的 ShioajiHistoryPage 帶 PossiblyTrafficExhausted 讓呼叫端分辨「沒有資料」與「流量用完」,並新增流量計 ShioajiTrafficMeter(每個回應的位元組數,按台北時間每日 08:00 重置,可與 GetUsageAsync 回報的用量對照);全市場日 OHLCV 的端點路徑與回應形狀文件都沒寫,屬未驗證推定,路徑可用 ShioajiOptions.DailyQuotesPath 覆寫;ShioajiContractClient 新增 ListAllContractsAsync 走完所有分頁。行程監督(ShioajiServerSupervisor)以環境變數把憑證直接餵給子行程,憑證不寫任何檔案、不進日誌,輸出逐行遮罩後才寫入日誌;外部已啟動的 server 以 Attach 模式接手而不干涉其行程,模式(模擬或正式)與設定不符時拒絕接手;行程非預期退出時以退避重啟,超過上限進入 Faulted。HTTP 用戶端不簽章、不限流(限流由本地預算負責),重試只對 GET,所有 POST(含下單、改價、改量、撤單、訂閱)絕不重試;下單的逾時與 5xx 在錯誤上標記「結果未知」,避免呼叫端誤判為沒下成功而重複下單。行情走官方聚合串流(GET /api/v1/stream/data,一條 SSE 連線帶全部事件):逐行解析 event 與 data,股票與期權的成交、五檔、報價、指數報價與委託回報各有型別,所有價格與數量一律以原始文字解析成 decimal(絕不經過 double),台北時間的 date 與 time 以固定 UTC+8 轉成 UTC;格式未知的心跳一律保留原文,事件名不認得的以 UnknownEvent 原樣送出;讀不懂的事件以失敗送出而不是靜默吞掉。斷線或閒置逾時以退避重連,重連後呼叫端注入的回呼可重放訂閱與委託回報訂閱;連線、斷線、重連以生命週期事件從同一個串流送出;佇列有界,滿了丟棄最舊的並計數。本地限流預算(行情查詢 10 秒 50 次、帳務 5 秒 25 次、委託 10 秒 250 次、訂閱上限 200)在請求到達券商之前先擋下,絕不讓請求打到券商的處置線。所有預期的失敗回傳 Result,錯誤碼一律 shioaji. 開頭並集中在 ShioajiErrorCodes。A .NET 10 client for the official local HTTP server of SinoPac's Shioaji (shioaji server start), built on the Ozakboy.Http pipeline and the Ozakboy.Security masker with no third-party community packages. This first milestone covers what a Taiwan stock day-trading desktop needs: starting and supervising the official server process, querying accounts and contracts, subscribing to market data and reading the stream, and placing and listing orders. Version 0.2.0 adds historical data (ShioajiHistoryClient): 1-minute bars, ticks, snapshots, the all-market daily OHLCV, the ranking scanner, short-stock sources, margin and short balances, and the disposition and attention lists; a 1-minute-bar range over 30 days and a snapshot over 500 contracts are refused locally; a "column-array" response (datetime[], Open[] and so on, one array per field) fails as a whole when any column's length differs, so half-filled data is never handed out; over the daily traffic allowance the broker does not fail but answers with empty values, so the returned ShioajiHistoryPage carries PossiblyTrafficExhausted to tell "no data" from "traffic spent", and a new traffic meter, ShioajiTrafficMeter (the bytes of every response, bucketed by Taipei day with a reset at 08:00 and comparable with the usage GetUsageAsync reports), is added; neither the endpoint path nor the response shape of the all-market daily OHLCV is documented, so they are unverified inferences and the path can be overridden with ShioajiOptions.DailyQuotesPath; ShioajiContractClient gains ListAllContractsAsync, which walks every page. The supervisor feeds credentials to the child process through environment variables only, so they never touch a file or a log, and every output line is masked before it is logged; an already-running server is attached to without managing its process, and refused when its simulation or production mode disagrees with the configuration; an unexpected exit is restarted with backoff until a limit puts the supervisor in Faulted. The HTTP client neither signs nor rate-limits (the local budget does that), retries GET only, and never retries a POST — orders, price and quantity changes, cancellations and subscriptions included; an order that times out or meets a 5xx is flagged with an unknown outcome so a caller does not mistake it for "not placed" and send it twice. Market data uses the official aggregate stream (GET /api/v1/stream/data, one SSE connection for every event): event and data lines are parsed one by one into typed ticks, order books, quotes, index quotes and order reports for stocks and futures/options, every price and quantity is parsed from its raw text into decimal and never through double, and the Taipei date and time are converted to UTC at a fixed UTC+8. A heartbeat of unknown format is kept verbatim, an event name that is not recognised surfaces as an UnknownEvent, and an event that cannot be read surfaces as a failure instead of being swallowed. A dropped connection or an idle timeout reconnects with backoff, a caller-injected callback replays subscriptions and the order-report subscription afterwards, connect, disconnect and reconnect arrive as lifecycle events on the same stream, and the queue is bounded, dropping the oldest and counting. A local rate budget (market queries 50 per 10 s, account queries 25 per 5 s, orders 250 per 10 s, at most 200 subscriptions) refuses before a request reaches the broker, so the broker's penalty line is never approached. Every expected failure is a Result whose code starts with shioaji. and lives in ShioajiErrorCodes.</Description>
    <PackageTags>ozakboy;tradekit;shioaji;sinopac;taiwan;stock;futures;day-trading;http;sse;server-sent-events;market-data;historical-data;kbars;snapshot;traffic;tick;order-book;order;order-event;supervisor;process;rate-limit;budget;reconnect;result-type;decimal;dotnet;csharp</PackageTags>

