    <PackageReleaseNotes>0.2.0 — Historical data and a traffic meter. New ShioajiHistoryClient: GetKbarsAsync (1-minute bars; a range over 30 calendar days, both ends counted, is refused locally with shioaji.history.range_too_long), GetTicksAsync (AllDay, RangeTime or LastCount), GetSnapshotsAsync (at most 500 contracts, otherwise shioaji.history.too_many_contracts), GetDailyQuotesAsync, GetScannerAsync, GetShortStockSourcesAsync, GetCreditEnquireAsync, GetRegulatoryPunishAsync and GetRegulatoryNoticeAsync; every call goes through the MarketQuery budget after its local checks. Results are ShioajiHistoryPage&lt;T&gt; {Items, ResponseBytes, IsEmpty, PossiblyTrafficExhausted}: over the daily traffic allowance the broker answers market queries with empty values instead of an error, so an empty page may mean exhausted traffic and not "no data". Column-array responses (kbars and ticks) are read by ShioajiColumnarReader: columns of unequal length fail the whole response with shioaji.history.malformed, a datetime is an ISO string (no offset means Taipei wall-clock time, fixed UTC+8) or an epoch in seconds, milliseconds, microseconds or nanoseconds by magnitude, and numbers are read from raw text into decimal, never double. ShioajiTrafficMeter (a singleton on a TimeProvider) records the bytes of every response (Content-Length, or the bytes read when chunked), buckets them by Taipei traffic day with the reset at 08:00, exposes TodayBytes, Reset and Snapshot, and receives the usage ShioajiAuthClient.GetUsageAsync reports as ServerReportedBytes. ShioajiContractClient.ListAllContractsAsync walks every page at 500 per page through the MarketQuery budget. ShioajiOptions.DailyQuotesPath overrides the path of the all-market daily OHLCV. UNVERIFIED: that path (default /api/v1/data/daily_quotes, awaiting confirmation against a real server's OpenAPI; the documentation mentions only the command line's `shioaji data daily-quotes`) and its response shape (assumed an array of objects with at least code, open, high, low, close and volume), the request bodies of short_stock_sources and credit_enquire, and the shapes of scanner, short_stock_sources, credit_enquire and the two regulatory lists. Constructor changes: ShioajiApiClient, ShioajiAuthClient and ShioajiContractClient take optional trailing parameters, so existing code keeps compiling. Still not run against a real server with valid credentials. 0.1.1 — Adjusted to what a real `shioaji server start --no-open` was measured to do on 2026-10-30 (fake credentials). The server is a foreground process that never detaches, so the "exits 0 while still answering" Attached path stays only as a defence. Its output carries ANSI colour codes: the supervisor now strips them line by line before logging and before keeping the last 20 lines. A failed login (output containing "Authentication failed", "login validation error", "invalid secret_key" or "invalid api_key") now returns the dedicated shioaji.server.auth_failed with the masked, stripped line in Error.Data["detail"], and goes straight to Faulted without entering the restart loop, also when it happens during a restart. The `server log: &lt;path&gt;` line printed at start is parsed into the new ShioajiServerStatus.LogFilePath (null when absent). ShioajiCredentials.Validate() and the supervisor now refuse a SecretKey containing characters outside base58 with shioaji.server.invalid_credentials before starting any process, echoing no character; ApiKey is not checked because its format is unknown. Behaviour change: a SecretKey that is not base58 used to start a process that then failed to log in, and now fails locally; ShioajiServerStatus gains the required LogFilePath property. 0.1.0 — First release. ShioajiServerSupervisor starts and supervises the official `shioaji server start --no-open` process (credentials only through child-process environment variables, never a file or a log; every output line masked; Attach mode for an already-running server; mode mismatch refused; backoff restarts up to a limit, then Faulted). ShioajiAuthClient, ShioajiContractClient, ShioajiQuoteClient and ShioajiOrderClient cover /api/v1/info, accounts, usage, stream status, subscribe_trade, contracts, market-data subscription, place_order, update_price, update_qty, cancel_order and trades. The pipeline neither signs nor rate-limits, retries GET only, and never retries a POST; an order that times out or meets a 5xx carries outcomeUnknown=true. ShioajiStreamReader reads the aggregate SSE stream into typed events (stock and futures/options tick, bid-ask and quote, index quote, order report, heartbeat, unknown, lifecycle) with idle detection, backoff reconnection, a post-reconnect replay callback, and a bounded queue that drops the oldest and counts. ShioajiRateBudget enforces market-query 50/10 s, account 25/5 s, order 250/10 s and at most 200 subscriptions locally. Prices and quantities are decimal parsed from raw JSON text, never double; Taipei date and time convert to UTC at a fixed +8. Not run against a real server: the heartbeat format, error-body shape and several response shapes are unmeasured and handled defensively. Not in this release: portfolio, historical data, combo orders, earmarking, watchlist, regulatory lists, and the neutral TradeKit.Abstractions mapping. Full notes: https://github.com/ozakboy/Ozakboy.TradeKit.Shioaji/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md</PackageReleaseNotes>

    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    這個命名空間幾乎每個檔案都用到(Result/Error),集中宣告成隱含 using,
    避免每個檔案開頭重複一行,也避免 XML 註解裡的 cref 反過來讓 IDE0005 判成未使用的 using。
    The namespace is used by almost every file, so it is declared once as an implicit using.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Using Include="Ozakboy.Core.Abstractions" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- 內部解析輔助型別需要直接測試,它們不屬於公開契約。 -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Ozakboy.TradeKit.Shioaji.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\logo.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    相依政策:只允許 .NET BCL、Microsoft 官方套件與 Ozakboy.* 自研套件,判定看「遞移相依」而非套件名稱。
    Ozakboy.TradeKit.Abstractions 0.8.0 本版只引用、不實作其介面(M1 再做中立介面的對映);
    引用它是為了讓 M1 升級時相依圖已經就位,而且它只帶 Ozakboy.Core.Abstractions。
    Ozakboy.Core.Abstractions 與 Ozakboy.Security 明確指定,不靠遞移帶進來:兩者的型別(Result、SecretMasker)
    都在本套件的公開契約上,上游哪天不再帶它,斷的會是本套件的編譯。
    Dependency policy: only the .NET BCL, first-party Microsoft packages, and Ozakboy.* packages, judged by the
    transitive graph. Ozakboy.TradeKit.Abstractions 0.8.0 is referenced but its interfaces are not implemented in
    this release (the neutral mapping is M1); referencing it now means the dependency graph is already in place at
    that upgrade, and it brings in nothing but Ozakboy.Core.Abstractions. Ozakboy.Core.Abstractions and
    Ozakboy.Security are pinned directly because their types (Result, SecretMasker) are on this package's public
    contract.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Ozakboy.TradeKit.Abstractions" Version="0.8.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Ozakboy.Http" Version="0.3.4" />
    <PackageReference Include="Ozakboy.Core.Abstractions" Version="0.3.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Ozakboy.Security" Version="0.1.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="10.0.14" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Http" Version="10.0.14" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="10.0.14" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    刻意不引用 Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub 套件,與其他 Ozakboy.* 套件一致(理由見 Binance 套件的 csproj)。
    SourceLink is deliberately not referenced as a package, in line with the other Ozakboy.* packages.
  -->

</Project>
